Hi ranger,

Bear Watch (<%= @site %>) has reached its Cloudflare R2 free-tier cap, so new
photo uploads are paused. Bear watchers now see:

  "Oops! Ran out of honey. A ranger needs to fix this."

What triggered it: <%= @trigger %>

Current usage:
<%= @usage_summary %>

Nothing will be charged: Bear Watch stops before going past the free tier.

To get uploads going again, do one of:
  - wait for next month (write/read limits reset on the 1st; storage doesn't),
  - delete old photos, or
  - raise R2_STORAGE_LIMIT_GB / R2_CLASS_A_LIMIT / R2_CLASS_B_LIMIT in .env
    (anything over the free tier is billed by Cloudflare) and restart.

Check usage any time with:
  docker compose exec web bin/rails bearwatch:storage:status

You'll get at most one of these emails per month.

-- Bear Watch
